  "name": "Repeated open-world kills of the same entry stop paying Bazaar Tokens after the cutoff",
  "contract": "At default settings (FactorPercent 67, RecoveryFactor 2, CutoffPercent 5) a level-20 player with open-world scaling on kills 14 Harvest Golems (entry 36, Westfall) one after another. The per-entry multiplier is 0.67^(kill-1), so the 9th kill's multiplier 0.67^8 is about 0.04, under the 5 percent cutoff: kills 9-14 pay exactly zero, which is deterministic. Eight Kobold Miners (entry 40) are then killed, each entry starting its own multiplier; the 16 kills together must pay at least once. The Creature roll is 0-2 and stochastic rounding also zeroes small amounts, so a single entry's first eight kills all paying zero has a few percent chance; across both entries it is about 0.1 percent. Per-entry recovery and entry independence are asserted deterministically by the bazaar_degression harness. Both entries have large, otherwise-unused open-world spawn pools so other Bazaar Token scenarios keep their living creatures.",
